{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הנוגע בנבלתם יטמא", :translit "ha-nogea b'nivlatam yitma", :gloss "the one touching their carcass shall become impure"} {:he "זה הנוגע אפילו בכעדשה", :translit "zeh ha-nogea afilu b'k'adasha", :gloss "this one who touches even like a lentil"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "הנוגע בנבלתם יטמא", :b "זה הנוגע אפילו בכעדשה"}], :frame {:text "The minimum quantity of animal carcass that conveys tum'ah by contact is a ke-adashah, the size of a lentil (Mishnah Kelim 17:6). This lentil-sized standard for carcass impurity is established in the halakhic midrash on this very verse, Leviticus 11:27 (Sifra, Shemini, parashah 5, chapter 4). The phrase 'even like a lentil' (af b'chulshehu in talmudic idiom) underscores that tum'ah is transmitted by contact with even a minuscule amount of the forbidden carcass.", :sources ["Mishnah Kelim 17:6" "Sifra Shemini parashah 5 chapter 4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "הנוגע בנבלתם יטמא", :a-value 718, :b "זה הנוגע אפילו בכעדשה", :b-value 674, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:56.549980845Z", :model "glm-5.2"}